summary:
  A stop no longer ends the network-back resume.

history:
  The parity invariant measures a park against a stop, so a line taken out
  of the stop shrinks the yardstick and both stay green. The stop is the
  road most people take and had no floor of its own until 2026-09-21:
  commenting this line out left the whole gate green.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
          healRetryTimer.stop();
          netResumeTimer.stop();
          // A stop inside the wake-tone window is the person saying "I'm up" —

replace:
          healRetryTimer.stop();
          netResumeTimer.interval = netResumeTimer.interval;
          // A stop inside the wake-tone window is the person saying "I'm up" —

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_stop_still_silences_everything_it_used_to.
  Line-neutral.
